RPi::WiringPi test platform GPIO pin connections

Left of '->' is the Pi BCM GPIO (or a signal/rail); right of '->' is the
destination. Numbers in (parens) on the right are the peripheral IC's own chip
pin, NOT a Pi GPIO. For the full diagram, the loop-back topology, the Pi-5
default pin states and the pin-collision analysis, see ../test-pinout.md.

Design note: the platform is self-verifying. Every output the library drives is
looped back into an ADC (or a sister port) so a test can measure what it drove
(see the loop-back lines below and ../test-pinout.md section 1).

# I2C bus (shared: GPIO2 = SDA, GPIO3 = SCL, one pull-up pair)

Addresses in use on the Pi I2C bus:

    0x04  Arduino Metro Mini       (t/300, t/305)
    0x05  ATMega-328P              (optional; only when in I2C mode)
    0x20  MCP23017 expander #1     (t/330)
    0x21  MCP23017 expander #2     (t/450, drives the stepper)
    0x3c  OLED SSD1306 128x64      (t/900-920; on the Pi I2C bus)
    0x48  ADS1115 ADC #1           (t/109, t/140, t/325, t/345)
    0x49  ADS1115 ADC #2           (t/450)
    0x57  AT24C32 EEPROM           (t/420-422; same board as the RTC)
    0x68  DS3231 RTC               (t/320)
    0x77  BMP180 pressure/temp     (t/340)

# LCD (HD44780, 4-bit; dedicated pins, skipped by the pin-status check)

5  -> RS
6  -> E
4  -> D4
17 -> D5
27 -> D6
22 -> D7

# ADS1115 ADC #1 (0x48) - analog read-back for the PWM-side devices

SDA -> SDA
SCL -> SCL
18  -> A0      (GPIO18 PWM/servo output looped back; t/109, t/140, t/325)
              A1 <- MCP4XXXX digital-pot wiper          (t/345, reads ch 1)

# ADS1115 ADC #2 (0x49) - stepper position sense

SDA -> SDA
SCL -> SCL
              A0 <- photoresistor (right)               (t/450, reads ch 0)
              A1 <- photoresistor (centre)              (t/450, reads ch 1)
              A2 <- photoresistor (left)                (t/450, reads ch 2)

# MCP3008 ADC (SPI; CS = GPIO26) - analog read-back for the SPI-side devices

11 -> 13 (SCLK)
9  -> 12 (MISO)
10 -> 11 (MOSI)
26 -> 10 (CS)
         CH1 <- MCP4922 DAC output 0                    (t/310)
         CH3 <- MCP4922 DAC output 1                    (t/310)
         CH2 <- 74HC595 Q-output                        (t/335)

# MCP4XXXX Digital Potentiometer (SPI; CS = GPIO13)

13 -> 1 (CS)
11 -> 2 (SCLK)
10 -> 3 (MOSI)
        wiper -> ADS1115 #1 (0x48) A1   (end terminals to 3V3 / GND reference)

# MCP4922 DAC (SPI; CS = GPIO12)

12 -> 3 (CS)
11 -> 4 (SCLK)
10 -> 5 (MOSI)
        out 0 -> MCP3008 CH1
        out 1 -> MCP3008 CH3

# 74HC595 Shift Register (outputs read back via MCP3008)

21 -> 14 (DATA/DS)
16 -> 12 (LATCH/ST_CP)
20 -> 11 (SHCP/SH_CP)
        Q-output -> MCP3008 CH2

# Serial (UART loopback; needs the primary UART freed from Bluetooth)

14 -> 15 (TXD -> RXD)

# DS3231 RTC (0x68) + AT24C32 EEPROM (0x57) - shared breakout board

SCL -> SCL
SDA -> SDA

# BMP180 barometric pressure / temperature (0x77)

SCL -> SCL
SDA -> SDA

# OLED SSD1306 128x64 (0x3c)

SCL -> SCL
SDA -> SDA

# MCP23017 GPIO Expander #1 (0x20) - Port A looped to Port B

SCL   -> SCL
SDA   -> SDA
3.3V+ -> 18 (Reset)      NOTE: chip pin 18 (active-low RESET) tied high; NOT GPIO18
A0 -> B0
A1 -> B1
A2 -> B2
A3 -> B3
A4 -> B4
A5 -> B5
A6 -> B6
A7 -> B7

# MCP23017 GPIO Expander #2 (0x21) - stepper driver

SCL   -> SCL
SDA   -> SDA
3.3V+ -> 18 (Reset)      NOTE: chip pin 18, tied high; NOT GPIO18
A0..A3 -> ULN2003 -> stepper coils 1-4   (Bank A pins 0-3; t/450)

# GPIO18 is multiplexed (see ../test-pinout.md section 6)

Used as the hardware PWM/servo output (t/109, t/140, t/325), a self-triggered
edge-interrupt input (t/200-212; edges generated by toggling the INTERNAL pull
resistor, so no external edge driver is wired), and a generic register/multi
test pin. Its only physical connection is to ADS1115 #1 A0. Keep this net free
of external pull resistors and loads or the interrupt tests will fail.
